42
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.640
Here's what we're talking about today.

43
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:29.280
It is Pam's Replacement, Season 8, Episode 7, written by Alison Silverman and directed by

44
00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:29.880
Matt Sohn.

45
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.480
Here's a summary.

46
00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:36.500
Frustrated that people are coddling her because she's pregnant, Pam and Dwight go to great

47
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:42.380
lengths to get Jim to admit that he finds Kathy, her temporary replacement, attractive.

48
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:48.940
Meanwhile, Kevin and the Zitz invite Robert California to join their jam session, but they are upstaged

49
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.500
when Robert and his former bandmates take over.

50
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.820
Why would Kevin want his band to be called Kevin and the Zitz?

51
00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:00.020
Who thinks the word zit sounds appealing or fun?

52
00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.880
I mean, why would Daryl and Andy want it to be called that?

53
00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.640
There's a zit.

54
00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.160
Well, I don't think they do.

55
00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:14.080
Fast fact number one, big guest star arc alert, Lindsay Broad as Kathy.

56
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.100
Yes.

57
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:20.040
We got a fan question from Michaela in Utah who said, I want to know everything about Lindsay

58
00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.700
Broad as she is introduced in this episode.

59
00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.600
Yes, Michaela, Lindsay is Pam's Replacement.

60
00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.720
And she appears in 12 episodes this season.

61
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.040
I slid into her DMs.

62
00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:36.500
And she is going to come on, Office Ladies, for our Tallahassee episode.

63
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.720
Oh my gosh, that's a big one for Kathy.

64
00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:40.380
I know.

65
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.120
That's going to be so great.

66
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.700
I can't wait to talk to her all about it.

67
00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:48.260
Well, I didn't get to work with her a lot because the majority of her time was when Pam

68
00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.060
was on maternity leave, but I thought she was fantastic.

69
00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.000
I mean, she's so good in this episode.

70
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.840
And then I remember she's also a very nice person, so.

71
00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.900
Well, my memory of Lindsay is that she just joined the show like seamless,

72
00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.780
she was amazing, cute as a button.

73
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.860
And you know what?

74
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.680
I mean, I have to think that if she was my replacement, I might be like, oh, well, that's

75
00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.960
a very adorable, beautiful gal that's going to be sitting next to my husband.

76
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.580
Well, that leads me very well into fast fact number two, Angela.

77
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.120
This episode was written by Allison Silverman-Jones.

78
00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.480
Allison was a new writer with us this season, and this was her first episode that she wrote.

79
00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.740
Allison is amazing.

80
00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.660
I absolutely loved her.

81
00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.700
And, you know, after The Office, she went on to be the executive producer of The Unbreakable

82
00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.080
Kimmy Schmidt, At Home with Amy Sedaris, and Russian Doll.

83
00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.160
I mean, she's a badass.

84
00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:40.740
Yes.

85
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.660
Before coming to The Office, she wrote on The Daily Show.

86
00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.600
She also wrote on Portlandia.

87
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.340
She's very funny.

88
00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:52.260
And when she was writing this episode, she was pregnant.

89
00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.100
That's right.

90
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:58.460
I was very excited because I was the first pregnant cast member, right?

91
00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:04.500
And then you, and then finally we had a pregnant woman in the writer's room.

92
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:04.940
Yes.

93
00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.240
She was the first female writer to then also be a parent.

94
00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:09.940
That's right.

95
00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.960
So we had a lot of dads in the writer's room.

96
00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:12.560
Yes, we did.

97
00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.740
This was our first mom.

98
00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.680
Well, we had a fan question from Ashley K.

99
00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:17.780
in Missouri who said,

100
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.760
I have been waiting for this episode to ask Jenna this question.

101
00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.960
In these episodes, Pam and Jenna are both pregnant, and I feel like some of the jokes

102
00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.080
are a little insensitive.

103
00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:32.960
I was super emotional when pregnant, and I'm not an actor, but did Jenna ever get her feelings

104
00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.620
hurt by some of the jokes about her pregnancy?

105
00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.620
I'll tell you what, Ashley.

106
00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.100
I did not.

107
00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:48.880
I thought that this episode was so well-written and so beautifully highlighted, some of those

108
00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:55.900
insecurities that you might have, and actually speaking honestly about them, which is really

109
00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.600
what Pam wants in this episode.

110
00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.860
When everybody is just, you know, feeding her a bunch of bull, she knows it.

111
00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:06.060
And she's like, no, we can just talk about me.

112
00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.380
I'm still like a person who is in reality.

113
00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:15.080
You know, Jenna, I saw this great comment after our rewatch of The List aired that I've

114
00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.240
been wanting to share with you, and I thought this episode was perfect to tell you.

115
00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:23.760
There was the photo of Angela Martin and Pam side by side, the big pregs, little pregs,

116
00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.060
right?

117
00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:24.440
Yes, right.

118
00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.420
And this woman wrote underneath it and said, you know what this is to me?

119
00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.120
It's not big pregs, little pregs.

120
00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.280
It's real life pregnant versus fake TV pregnant.

121
00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:40.160
And I thought that was great because, like you said, we're seeing a real pregnancy shown.

122
00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.180
You know, my pregnancy was not shown.

123
00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:47.400
They got really creative in hiding it, but I thought this was so great to see a real woman

124
00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.400
really pregnant.

125
00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.000
And Allison and I talked about that.

126
00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:56.200
You know, one of the great things about having a person who was pregnant write this episode

127
00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:59.000
was that we got it, you know?

128
00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:02.000
So talk about representation in the writer's room.

129
00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.760
You're not in that club till you're in that club, and then you're like, oh, this club.

130
00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:06.200
Yes.

131
00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:06.480
Yeah.

132
00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:11.400
So I'll talk a little more specifically about some of the scenes that I found especially

133
00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.300
awesome as we get to them.

134
00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:18.820
But overall, my feelings were not hurt by anything that was said, and I loved this episode.

135
