00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:27.860
And when we get back, we have a cringola of a cold open.

205
00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.140
I want to just say something.

206
00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:31.400
This might be a bold statement.

207
00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:37.040
I think now the character that makes me sometimes the most uncomfortable is Erin.

208
00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:41.580
Yeah, she's taken over where Michael left off.

209
00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:42.320
Maybe so.

210
00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:53.170
This episode starts with Andy.

211
00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:54.590
He's running up to front reception.

212
00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:58.830
He's going to say, Erin, listen, in two minutes, I want you to pretend to call me.

213
00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:03.790
Say it's an important call, but I am not going to take the call because I want this client

214
00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:07.130
who I'm meeting with to know how important he is.

215
00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.070
So I won't take the important call.

216
00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.070
She's immediately confused.

217
00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:13.150
Yeah, she says, who's calling?

218
00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.030
He's like, there's no one's calling.

219
00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:15.630
He's like, no one's calling.

220
00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.310
And she goes, but you're not going to take it.

221
00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:18.410
He's like, oh, my God.

222
00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:22.110
Andy, I'm like, Andy, right away, you should bail on this.

223
00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:22.890
Right away.

224
00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:27.090
They spend a lot of time going back and forth until Erin gets it.

225
00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:30.730
I was actually impressed that we stayed on this for so long.

226
00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:31.850
It made it even funnier.

227
00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:32.850
It's hilarious.

228
00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:37.070
But if you're Andy, you're like, how many red flags do you need

229
00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.930
before you know this is not going to work?

230
00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.070
Well, it's not going to work.

231
00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:45.050
Andy starts his meeting with the client, played by Dave Anthony.

232
00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:50.750
He is a comedian, podcaster, and writer on the series Marin and also on Deadly Class.

233
00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:52.590
Erin's going to come in.

234
00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:53.030
Yeah.

235
00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:54.390
Andy, you have a phone call.

236
00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.410
It's very important.

237
00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.350
He's like, well, I'm not going to take it.

238
00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:58.430
I'm with an important client.

239
00:10:58.610 --> 00:10:58.710
Yeah.

240
00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:00.590
Nothing's more important than my client.

241
00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:03.650
And then she says, well, your mom's dead.

242
00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.330
She was hit by a bus.

243
00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:07.870
He's like, she's not really dead.

244
00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:08.830
Yeah, yeah, she's dead.

245
00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:13.510
Well, that little look that Ellie gives to camera after she says, your mom is dead, was

246
00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:14.130
scripted.

247
00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.350
It's wonderful.

248
00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:17.590
Andy really doesn't know what to do.

249
00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:22.270
And then he gets a phone call from a state trooper who is Daryl.

250
00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:24.390
